overnment  has taken have been inadequate the  comments came as trudeau was asked  why his government is launching another  investigation just  six years after the deshaun report done  under the previous harper government  describe the culture within the military  as hostile  and endemic  survivors continue to feel that they are  not appropriately  supported continue to feel like the only  thing they can do  is either talk to the media or come  forward anonymously  and that is a failing of the entire  system  trudeau says his government will look to  make immediate changes  while former supreme court justice louis  arbor conducts her work  the toronto blue jays say they're  cutting all ties with hall of famer  roberto alamar  after a sexual misconduct investigation  the investigation was launched after an  industry employee came forward with an  allegation from 2014.  major league baseball says it reviewed  the findings and found  alamar had violated league policies he's  now been placed  on mlb's ineligible list and the blue  jays say they're taking down his banner  at the rogers center alamar said in a  statement today he's disappointed  surprised and upset  with the news it was a joyful  celebration that became a  mass tragedy coming up what went wrong  at a religious festival  in israel  45 people including at least two  canadians have been killed in a stampede  in israel  and a warning some of the story contains  disturbing images  tens of thousands of mostly  ultra-orthodox jews had gathered to  celebrate  lag ba omer it was the first mass  religious gathering held in israel since  the country eased its covet 19  restrictions witnesses say the stampede  started when a large number of people  tried to exit the festival through a  narrow tunnel-like passage  it's a difficult moment and it's going  to be a difficult next couple of days  members of montreal's jewish community  have confirmed the canadian victims  are 21 year old devi steinmetz as well  as well-known singer  shraga gestetner  a shot for a shot still ahead creative  paths to  covet immunity in the united states  the situation in india remains dire as  the country struggles to deal with a  surge in covet 19 cases  india set another global record today  recording more than 385 thousand new  confirmed cases  in the last 24 hours more than 3 400  people  have died daily deaths have nearly  tripled in the past three weeks  hospitals are still overwhelmed and they  are still struggling to deal with  oxygen shortages but india is now facing  a new problem  a lack of vaccines several indian states  have run out of doses forcing them to  shut down  mass vaccination centers the u.s  meantime is facing a much different  problem  it has lots of vaccine supply but not  enough demand  tens of thousands of vaccine  appointments are going unfilled across  the country  the number of doses administered each  day in the u.s is dropping  and as jackson proskow explains that's  forcing some states to get creative  to convince vaccine skeptics to get the  shot  i am here at our large-scale vaccination  clinic  and as you can see we have lots of empty  chairs for all the vaccine available to  americans  the supply of willing recipients is  starting to dwindle  this is going to be an uphill battle i  really kind of see us in this time  crunch of  trying to get people vaccinated before  we see some of these other variants  100 million people are now fully  vaccinated more than half the population  has received at least one shot  and yet the rate of inoculation has  slowed dramatically down 25  in the last week to an average 2.5  million doses per day  we have to get to that 75  80 percent of us fully vaccinated  and really get this thing under control  there's little room for error because  one quarter of americans say they're  vaccine hesitant and will not get the  shot  i do not plan on getting it unless i am  forced  to change the game states are getting  creative  in louisiana a shot for shots program is  making its way through bars  well the convenience is what spoke to me  most today the fact that it's literally  five feet away from me  i work late nights i've either just  never found the time or just been too  exhausted to go out  some nba teams are planning to offer  vaccines to fans during games  and mobile clinics are fanning out  across communities  to meet people where they are getting as  many americans  vaccinated as efficiently and equitably  as possible is our path to returning  to a more normal lifestyle the next 100  million shots will be much tougher to  administer  but no less important the u.s still  averages more than 50  000 new infections each day each of us  needs to look around  in our communities and our families and  our circle of friends  and ask people if they have a plan to  get vaccinated the hope is that trusted  local voices like doctors and pastors  can help convince skeptics as  communities do all they can to get shots  into arms  jackson prosko global news washington  and new real world data shows the  benefits of vaccination  a u.s cdc study found those who were  given two doses of either the pfizer  biontec or moderna vaccine  were 94 percent less likely to be  hospitalized than those  who were not vaccinated but the efficacy  dropped to just 64 percent  if they only had one shot researchers  found  no significant effectiveness for people  who were less than 14 days past their  first dose  highlighting that it takes time for the  vaccine benefits to kick in  the findings are consistent with vaccine  clinical trials  it's the only night i didn't say i love  you because i thought i would have the  very next day  but kovid killed her husband with no  warning  that's next  we end tonight with a story of just how  cruel  covid19 can be we often report on the  statistics of the virus  the numbers of cases and dead but behind  each number is a person a british  columbia woman who lost her  young healthy husband to covet 19 is  sharing her family's heartbreaking story  and as ahmad agahi reports she hopes her  tragedy will serve as a warning  to all canadians he poured everything he  poured everything  into being a father from all the  memories they've shared  [Music]  who would have known these tragic  haunting moments  would be the last i just said okay good  night  come on that's the only night that i  didn't say i love you  it's the only night i've said i love you  every single night prior to that  it's the only night i didn't say i love  you because i thought i would have the  very next day  her husband 46 year old reed hans who  was diagnosed with covid19  10 days prior had a fever a cough  it was more comfortable for him to sleep  on the couch that night  and that's where he would struggle to  take his last breath  i went over just to say good morning  and then i put my hand on his arm  put my hand on his arm it was cold  and then when i tried to move his arm i  couldn't move his arm  so that i was like shaking him i'm  reading wake up marie wake up  and then it wasn't until i moved his  eyelids back and then i saw that he was  unresponsive so then i called 9-1-1  what happened next was a blur she says  until it was time to speak to her  children  i said okay i have something to tell you  about dad and you know right away i  don't know who was it that said it but  he said  is he dead and i said yes you know my  older one he's ten  and he just he just collapsed and he  just starts crying  and i think my eight-year-old he was sad  but i don't think he knew what to do and  he started crying because his brother  was  crying and so as boys  do you want to come over and you want to  say goodbye you know it's  not scary daddy just looks like he's  sleeping and they both said yes  i said okay so i walk them over and he's  still there lying peacefully and  they come in and my little guy comes  over and he's just like bye dad i love  you  like that was it like that was okay my  